* text=auto eol=lf
*.im text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.md text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.c text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.h text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.js text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.json text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# `src/mod/gui_mod.c` is stored in the index WITH CRLF while the `* text=auto
# eol=lf` rule above tells git to materialise it as LF.  The two disagree, so
# every fresh checkout wants to rewrite the file: a brand-new worktree reports
# ` M src/mod/gui_mod.c` and `git diff --stat` shows the same 3932 lines added
# and removed.  That noise makes tools/stream.sh call a clean stream dirty.
# Keep this one file byte-for-byte as stored (see docs/BOARD.md §7).
src/mod/gui_mod.c text eol=crlf

